.TH SINDOOK-CONTACTS 1 "2026-08-15" "sindook 0.5.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
sindook-contacts \- save and use named recipient public keys
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sindook contacts
[\fBlist\fP [\fB\-json\fP] | \fBadd\fP [\fB\-f\fP] \fINAME\fP
\fIPUBLIC_KEY_OR_FILE\fP | \fBshow\fP \fINAME\fP | \fBremove\fP \fINAME\fP]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Saves shareable recipient public keys under portable,
case-insensitive names. Use a saved contact anywhere a recipient is
accepted, for example \fB\-r @alice\fP. The configuration file
contains public keys and an optional default identity path only; it
never contains private keys or passphrases.
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
.B list
list saved contacts (with \fB\-json\fP: one JSON array)
.TP
\fBadd\fP [\fB\-f\fP] \fINAME\fP \fIPUBLIC_KEY_OR_FILE\fP
save a public key under \fINAME\fP; \fB\-f\fP replaces an existing
contact
.TP
\fBshow\fP \fINAME\fP
print one saved public key
.TP
\fBremove\fP \fINAME\fP
delete a saved contact
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
sindook contacts add alice alice.key.pub
sindook contacts add finance-team team.keys
sindook contacts list
sindook seal -r @alice report.pdf
sindook contacts remove alice
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR sindook (1),
.BR sindook-paths (1),
.BR sindook-seal (1)
